{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1504261-river-magic-homebrew-bits-and-bobs","id":1504261,"title":"River Magic Homebrew (bits and bobs)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-03-03T06:52:23-08:00","id":1504261,"title":"River Magic Homebrew (bits and bobs)","content":"In my Cincinnati based game my PCs recently did a big favor for Coursing Murky River, spirit of the Ohio River and the most powerful and influential nature spirit in the area. They ferreted out which of her vassals was building a powerbase of Shadow Occultists in an attempt to eventually supplant her (Fetid Ooze, spirit of river contaminants) and they subdued that spirit. Returning the favor, CMR gave them some talens that looked like large clear orbeez, and agreed to teach them river magics. She also agreed to bind her treacherous underling into a fetish, rather than destroying him.<br /> <br /> I had to do a bit of homebrew here, both for the river magics, and the items. If anyone spots anything wrong here feel free to critique but honestly I was mostly just excited I'd made some homebrew and wanted to share.<br /> <br /> For the magics I am giving them access to learn the Gift of Rivers, most of which I'm ripping off of Acrozatarim's excellent Gift of the Sea (which can be found on his Patreon), but the Honor gift is all about the prey getting lost, adrift on the sea, which I thought wasn't very Rivery and so I made this Honor facet:<br /> <br /> <b>Path to the River's Mouth (Honor)</b> <br /> Like debris caught in the flow of a river, the prey is inexorably pushed by currents too powerful to swim against. Just like the debris eventually reaches the mouth of the river, the prey will find itself where the current of the Uratha's essence ends.<br /> <br /> Cost: 2 essence<br /> <br /> Dice Pool: Wits + Survival + Honor - Prey's Resolve<br /> <br /> Action: Instant<br /> <br /> Duration: Until the prey reaches the destination, or one month, whichever comes first<br /> <br /> The Uratha may target any prey they can perceive and select a specific location, object or individual that the Uratha is aware of. Currents of essence sweep the prey toward that individual.<br /> <br /> Dramatic Failure: The Uratha suffers the Ban Condition, and must travel to the indicated destination themselves, at the earliest opportunity.<br /> <br /> Failure: The facet fails.<br /> <br /> Success: The target finds itself pulled toward the specified destination. Any time the prey attempts to travel a significant distance (walking to the kitchen wouldn't count, but driving to work, or even to the convenience store a block a way, would) they must roll Resolve + Survival - the Uratha's Honor. On a failure they instead travel toward the Uratha's chosen destination without noticing. After (Honor) hours of travel the prey may notice that they're headed in the wrong direction and try to right themselves, attempting another roll as above to go to their desired destination.<br /> <br /> Exceptional Success: Double the penalty and number of hours the prey will travel before noticing what they're doing.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> I also created a rite and wrote up a specific version of the Shadowbind rite:<br /> <br /> <b>Shadowbind</b> <br /> <br /> Grooves are carved into the ground in a pattern that incorporates first tongue sigils that relate to the nature of the spirit and the key to break the binding. Then the ritemaster chants a series of orders to remain in place to the spirit while pouring water from the river into the grooves, which will remain as long as the rite holds, regardless of humidity or temperature levels.<br /> <br /> New rite:<br /> <br /> <b>Curse of the River's Rejection</b><br /> <br /> With this rite, the ritemaster seeks to turn a natural source of water against her prey, preventing the prey from drawing any nourishment from it.<br /> <br /> Symbols: The water source, the prey, befoulment, lies<br /> <br /> Sample Rite:<br /> <br /> The ritemaster pours poison into the river, lake or pond in question whispering apologies to the smallest spirits of the water to stavr off yheir Finally she gives the water a piece of her prey (blood, hair, or skin will all do) to focus its hate and spite on.<br /> <br /> Roll (Manipulation + Subterfuge) <br /> Action: Extended (10 successes; each roll represents minute); resisted by the Prey's stamina<br /> <br /> Duration: One month<br /> <br /> For the duration of the rite the prey can't quench their thirst with any water that comes from the cursed source, but other than faintly smelling of the ritemaster (exclusively to the prey) the water tastes, feels and smells perfectly normal to the prey. Most human prey will eventually succumb to dehydration, though bottled water may let the prey unwittingly stave off death for a few days. An Uratha or Shartha is more likely to notice the smell of a werewolf in their tap water, and may learn the significance of such, hunt down the ritemaster or both<b>.</b><br /> <br /> Finally I wrote up the fetish and talen:<br /> <br /> <b>Fetid Tendril</b><br /> <br /> Uses Strength + Weaponry to attack (+1 Lethal damage)<br /> <br /> Activated with a Resolve + Composure roll with a -3 penalty or by spending an essence.<br /> <br /> Enemies damaged by the whip while it is active must succeed on a Stamina + Primal Urge (or Resistance) roll with a -3 penalty or suffer the Sickness Tilt for the remainder of the scene.<br /> <br /> <b>River Pearls</b><br /> <br /> A bead of gelatinous river water the size of a lime, when smashed against a hard surface they spread out into a roughly circular sheet of rippling water a bit larger than a person. After a few seconds it settles and then becomes a portal to a place somewhere at the bottom of the Ohio River for the remainder of the scene. This will result in a large amount of river water flooding the area, potentially resulting in a death trap of done in a confined space. Additionally a strong swimmer can use this portal to escape into the river.<br /> <br /> Aiming for a particular location when throwing the talen requires a dexterity + athletics roll.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25805-gsv_fotnmc","name":"GSV_FOtNMC","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}